  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Amateur brass choirs of German Protestant parishes, which go back to the trombone choirs of the Moravian Brethren at Herrnhut in the eighteenth century and grew into a mass movement during the nineteenth-century revival in Minden-Ravensberg, Westphalia. Johannes Kuhlo of Bethel near Bielefeld shaped its repertoire of four-part chorale settings and its non-transposing notation, and the choirs play in services, at open-air and tower music and at large church festivals.",
